     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Lowers warfarin effect (the anticoagulant dose may need adjusting) and may reduce oral contraceptive effectiveness (a second form of birth control may be indicated). With alcohol: nausea, vomiting, flushing, tachycardia and severe hypotension have been reported."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
